  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile with avgpool aggregation (config_024, 0.629 acc) dramatically outperforms single-profile multimodal (config_022, 0.535 acc), a +9.4 pt gain. This makes the aggregation strategy the most critical unexplored design axis within the multiprofile setting. Config_026 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping all other settings identical to the best result (PCA_n2000, ViT-L, concat fusion). This directly tests whether a learned, attention-based aggregation can capture inter-profile dependencies that simple averaging misses. If transformer aggregation improves performance, it identifies a new lever for further gains; if it matches or underperforms avgpool, it confirms that profile averaging is sufficient and redirects budget toward RNA encoder choice or fusion strategy. Under a limited budget, this single-variable extension of the best-known configuration maximizes information per experiment about the most impactful remaining design decision."
}

